   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The purpose of c3 is to prepare d4, slicing away the bishop's control of the f2-square. It looks to weaken the d3-pawn, but Black has no central pawns left to exploit it. Against everything, the recipe is d4; the one prophylactic move Black has is the bishop to b6 to stop it, and then we support the centre with the knight to d2 and always meet a knight to g4 with d4. And never fear the pawn break c5 — the knight to c4 answers it every time, keeping our centre intact.",
   "kind": "review",
   "teaches": [
    "c3 prepares d4",
    "meet Ng4 with d4",
    "answer c5 with Nc4"
   ],
